# How To Use This Backend In Any Project

Any frontend

↓

Call

```http
POST /auth/register
```

↓

OTP sent

↓

Call

```http
POST /auth/verify-otp
```

↓

User verified

↓

Call

```http
POST /auth/login
```

↓

Receive JWT

↓

Store JWT

↓

Call

```http
GET /auth/me
Authorization: Bearer <token>
```

Works with

* React
* Next.js
* Vue
* Angular
* Flutter
* Android
* iOS
* Node
* Any backend
* Any frontend

because everything communicates over HTTP.

---

# Frontend Integration

Frontend only needs to call your API.

Example

```text
React
      │
fetch()
      │
Cloudflare Worker
```

Example endpoint

```javascript
fetch("https://your-worker.workers.dev/auth/register")
```

No frontend imports backend files directly.

Only API calls.

---

# Reusing In Future Projects

For a new project:

1. Deploy this backend.
2. Configure:

   * D1
   * Brevo
   * JWT Secret
3. Point the frontend to the backend URL.
4. Use the authentication endpoints.

You do NOT copy business logic into every project.

Every project shares the same authentication backend.

---

# Long-Term Vision

This backend should eventually become:

```text
@your-name/universal-auth
```

or

```text
@pixelrise/auth
```

An npm package or reusable service that can power authentication for all your future applications.

The only things that should vary between projects are configuration values (database binding, secrets, email provider settings), not the authentication logic itself.









